Z||000000||FieroJoe||12-23-2000||10:26 PM||||First off, I finally got my power lock system that I bought to work, just hooked up in my basement to a car battery, only to find out that the brand new, in the AC delco wrapper and all, left hand switch will only make the connection if you press super hard. arrrrrrr.<P>I paid 5.70 for it I think, and I dont think they will let me return it becuause technically it works fine......<P>but, I went to <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com," TARGET=_blank>www.gmpartsdirect.com,</A>  and found that I can have it for 3.25, which isnt bad at all for a new power lock switch.  But I was also curious about how much my exterior dew strips were that I got from the dealership.  I paid about 37.50 ea from Pontiac, where this place will sell them for only $18.00!  Man that makes me mad.<P>Before anybody goes to the dealer's for any gm part, find the part # and check this place out!!!<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||8
